fact WorkItem(id: "WI-728", description: some(value: "WI-714 follow-up: enforce negate's MEMBERSHIP-relation operand at LOAD time, not only at runtime. CONTEXT: proposal 052 / WI-714 negate increment (ac5f8a8d). negate(r) builds the negation(query: r.query) LogicalQuery, which the resolver lowers to NAF. NAF over a relation with a FREE column FLOUNDERS (the resolver cannot decide not p(?x) with ?x unbound, resolve.rs:993) -> a silent wrong answer, so the operand must be a MEMBERSHIP relation (0 columns: a bare 0-column rule, or an applied relation binding every column). GAP: that requirement is enforced only by the HOST BUILTIN at runtime (relation_negate rejects a non-empty columns set). The SIGNATURE cannot express it today: 'operation negate(r: Relation) -> Relation[T = Unit, E = r.E]' leaves the operand's T unconstrained because the arg-vs-param check SKIPS a non-ground param (validate_arg_against_param, typing.rs:14913), and pinning E to make the param ground both over-narrows E and trips a param-order canonicalization in types_compatible. So 'negate(person_name)' (a 1-column relation) type-checks and fails only when the stream is pulled. Note this is the single-param case: an op with 2+ params of the SAME parameterized sort gets cross-param consistency FREE via the op-type-params tie (enforce_member_tie) -- which is why union's schema match needs no custom check but negate's T=Unit does. FIX DIRECTION: a dedicated load-time operand-SCHEMA check (the typer knows the operand's Relation[T] schema at the call site -- T=Unit iff 0 columns), raised as a LOAD error naming the offending columns and pointing at the fix (bind the columns via application, or project/exists). Keep it GENERAL per the feedback-typer-no-nongeneric-code discipline -- do NOT key it on op_sym == Relation.negate; express it as a checkable constraint the signature carries (the Without/Concat type-constructor precedent: a type-level predicate the return-type normalization boundary reduces). ACCEPTANCE: negate(person_name) (1 free column) is a LOAD error, not a runtime one; negate(has_alice) (0 columns) still loads and runs; the existing wi714 negate tests stay green; nothing in the typer keyed on negate's identity; cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-714"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-08-16T19:47:18Z"))
